      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xv-6-ahzek-ahriman-source" hidden="true">
          <description>Ahzek Ahriman | 5 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 3 | 10 | 2+/4+
Force Organisation:
• HQ
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Artificer Armour
• Iron Halo
• Black Staff of Ahriman
• Bolt pistol
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons)
• Independent Character
• Master of the Legion
• Psyker (Mastery Level 3\)
• Corvidae
• Chief Librarian
• Ahriman's Cabal
RESTRICTION
Ahriman may only be included in a Thousand Sons army of 1,500 points or more.
OPTIONS
• Ahriman may take:
• Krak grenades .................................. +2 points
CORVIDAE Ahriman always belongs to the Corvidae and may not select another Prosperine Cult. He receives both the Corvidae Cult Arcana and Cult Mastery benefits. CHIEF LIBRARIAN Ahriman knows every psychic power in the ProHammer Divination discipline. He does not randomly select or choose a limited number of Divination powers before the battle. Ahriman still follows the normal ProHammer restrictions governing how many psychic powers a Psyker may successfully invoke during a player turn. BLACK STAFF OF AHRIMAN The Black Staff is a Master-crafted Prosperine Force Weapon. Once during each player turn, Ahriman may re-roll one failed Psychic Test. The second result must be accepted. If the re-rolled Psychic Test also fails, Ahriman suffers Perils of the Warp in addition to any other normal consequences. Activating the Black Staff as a Force Weapon does not count as invoking a psychic power. AHRIMAN'S CABAL Ahriman may select one Legion Command Squad as his personal retinue. The squad does not occupy a separate Force Organisation slot. A Command Squad selected in this manner may purchase Ahriman's Cabal for +50 points. AHRIMAN'S CABAL A unit upgraded to Ahriman's Cabal: • becomes a Brotherhood of Psykers (Mastery Level 2); • is assigned to the Corvidae; • receives both the Corvidae Cult Arcana and Cult Mastery; • selects two psychic powers from the ProHammer Divination discipline. The Cabal remains a separate Psyker from Ahriman. Ahriman's Mastery Level, Leadership and psychic powers are not combined with those of the Brotherhood. Any model in Ahriman's Cabal permitted to purchase a Power Weapon may upgrade that Power Weapon to a Prosperine Force Weapon for +5 points. The Cabal follows the normal Psychic Brotherhood rules for activating Force Weapons.</description>
        </rule>
      <rule id="r18-final-ahriman-corvidae" name="Corvidae" hidden="false"><description>Ahriman always belongs to the Corvidae and may not select another Prosperine Cult. He receives both the Corvidae Cult Arcana and Cult Mastery benefits.</description></rule><rule id="r18-final-ahriman-chief" name="Chief Librarian" hidden="false"><description>Ahriman knows every psychic power in the ProHammer Divination discipline. He does not randomly select or choose a limited number of Divination powers before the battle, but still follows the normal ProHammer limit on powers successfully invoked during a player turn.</description></rule><rule id="r18-final-ahriman-staff" name="Black Staff of Ahriman" hidden="false"><description>Master-crafted Prosperine Force Weapon. Once during each player turn Ahriman may re-roll one failed Psychic Test; the second result must be accepted. If the re-rolled test also fails, he suffers Perils of the Warp in addition to the normal consequences. Activating the Black Staff as a Force Weapon does not count as invoking a psychic power.</description></rule><rule id="r18-final-ahriman-div-rule-r61-librarian-power1-divination-prescience-rule" name="Prescience" hidden="false">
                          <description>Target friendly unit may re-roll all failed To Hit rolls.</description>
                        </rule>
                      <rule id="r18-final-ahriman-div-rule-r61-librarian-power1-divination-foreboding-rule" name="Foreboding" hidden="false">
                          <description>The Psyker and any joined unit gain Counter-Attack and may make Reaction Fire using the full number of allowed shots.

Counter-Attack: If this unit is not engaged with any enemy models and an enemy unit successfully completes a charge move against it, the unit may take a Leadership test. If passed, this unit gains +1 Attack during the Assault phase.</description>
                        </rule>
                      <rule id="r18-final-ahriman-div-rule-r61-librarian-power1-divination-forewarning-rule" name="Forewarning" hidden="false">
                          <description>Target friendly unit gains a 4+ Invulnerable Save.</description>
                        </rule>
                      <rule id="r18-final-ahriman-div-rule-r61-librarian-power1-divination-perfect-timing-rule" name="Perfect Timing" hidden="false">
                          <description>The Psyker and any joined unit ignore Cover when shooting an enemy unit.</description>
                        </rule>
                      <rule id="r18-final-ahriman-div-rule-r61-librarian-power1-divination-precognition-rule" name="Precognition" hidden="false">
                          <description>The Psyker re-rolls failed To Hit and To Wound rolls and failed saving throws.</description>
                        </rule>
                      <rule id="r18-final-ahriman-div-rule-r61-librarian-power1-divination-misfortune-rule" name="Misfortune" hidden="false">
                          <description>All attacks against the target enemy unit count as Rending.</description>
                        </rule>
                      </rules>
